1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was an Equestrian from Reate in the Sabine region of Italy. He served as a customs official in the province of Asia, where he was honored with statues dedicated "To an Honest Tax-gatherer", and later as a banker
2 CONC  among the Helvetii in Gaul, where he died. With his wife, Vespasia Pollio, he had two sons, Titus Flavius Sabinus and the future emperor Titus Flavius Vespasianus (aka Vespasian), and a daughter who died in infancy
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia:
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Titus_Flavius_Sabinus_I '''Titus Flavius Sabinus'''] (c. 20 BC - aft. 9, fl. 1st century BC to 1st century AD) was the son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Titus-Flavius-Petro/6000000013205685076 Titus 
2 CONC Flavius Petro] and wife [http://www.geni.com/people/Tertulla/6000000006101312593 ... Tertulla].
2 CONT
2 CONT He was an Equestrian from Reate (modern Rieti) in the Sabine region of Italy. He served as a customs official and then as a banker in the customs in the province of Asia, where he was honoured with statues dedicated "To an Honest 
2 CONC Tax-gatherer", and later as a banker at Aventicum among the Helvetii in Gaul, where he died.
2 CONT
2 CONT With his wife, [http://www.geni.com/people/Vespasia-Polla/6000000005241731148 Vespasia Polla], he had two sons, the consul [http://www.geni.com/people/Titus-Flavius-Sabinus/6000000013204919137 Titus Flavius Sabinus] and the future
2 CONC  emperor [http://www.geni.com/people/Vespasian-Emperor-of-Rome/6000000000701024840 Vespasian], and a daughter who died in infancy, [http://www.geni.com/people/Flavia-Vespasia-Sabinus/6000000010111470081 Flavia Vespasia].
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Tacitus, ''Histories''
2 CONT * Suetonius, ''On the Life of the Caesars''
2 CONT * Cassius Dio, ''Roman History''
2 CONT * Arnold Blumberg (ed) (1995), ''Great Leaders, Great Tyrants?: Contemporary Views of World Rulers Who Made History''
2 CONT
