2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Titus Flavius Sabinus=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Titus Flavius T. f. Sabinus was the father of the emperor Vespasian.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sabinus was the son of Titus Flavius Petro and his wife, Tertulla, and was an eques from Reate in the Sabine region of Italy. He served as a customs official and then as a banker in the province of Asia, where he was honoured with
2 CONC  statues dedicated "To an Honest Tax-gatherer", and later as a banker at Aventicum among the Helvetii in Gaul, where he died.
2 CONT
2 CONT With his wife, Vespasia Polla, he had at least two sons, the consul Titus Flavius Sabinus, and Titus Flavius Vespasianus, the future emperor Vespasian; and also a daughter who died in infancy, Flavia Vespasia. He may have had an e
2 CONC lder son, who was the father of Titus Flavius Sabinus, consul in AD 69.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Titus_Flavius_Sabinus_(father_of_Vespasian)
