2 CONT
2 CONT Flavius Liberalis was a Roman of the 1st century and was a man of equestrian rank, who came from Ferentium (modern Ferento) a country town in Italy. This man of humble origins was a quaestor and later a law clerk.
2 CONT
2 CONT Liberalis had his daughter Flavia Domitilla appear before a board of arbitration to prove her claim for Roman Citizenship, instead of a Latin one. She later married the future Emperor Vespasian. Her children with Vespasian were Do
2 CONC mitilla the Younger and Emperors Titus and Domitian.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
