1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lucius Aemilius Paullus (born before 29 BC – 14 AD) was the son of Paullus Aemilius Lepidus (suffect consul 34 BC and later censor) and Cornelia, the elder daughter of Scribonia. He was married to Julia the Younger
2 CONC , the eldest granddaughter of the Emperor Augustus.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucius_Aemilius_Paullus_(consul_1)
2 CONT
2 CONT For other persons named Lucius Aemilius Paullus, see Lucius Aemilius Paullus.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Life and Career
2 CONT
2 CONT Paullus' mother died sometime between 20 and 15 BC, and he was brought up by his widower father, Paullus Aemilius Lepidus. Sometime after 13 BC, this elder Paullus married Claudia Marcella Minor, who herself was a widow with a sma
2 CONC ll child.
2 CONT
2 CONT The early career of the younger Paullus is unknown, his first and only known post being that of consul in 1 with his brother-in-law, Gaius Caesar. He is also known to have been a member of the Arval Brethren[1].
2 CONT
2 CONT According to ancient historians, his wife Julia was exiled in 8 AD for having an affair with a senator. Paullus himself was executed as a conspirator in a revolt at some point between 1 and 14[2].
2 CONT
2 CONT He only had one child by his wife - a girl named Aemilia Lepida (4/3 BC-53 AD), who was betrothed to Claudius until the downfall of her parents caused her great-grandfather, Augustus, to break off the betrothal and marry her to Ma
2 CONC rcus Junius Silanus (consul 19), by whom she had several children[3].
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucius_Aemilius_Paullus_(consul_1)
