2 CONT Marcus Vipsanius Agrippa was a Roman statesman, general and architect. He was a close friend, son-in-law, and lieutenant to Emperoro Augustus and was responsible for the construction of some of the most beautiful buildings in the 
2 CONC history of Rome.
