1 NOTE Marcus Vipsanius Agrippa (63-12 BC) Roman commander and statesman. His third wife was Julia, daughter of the emperor Augustus, whom he helped to gain power. He defeated Sextus, the son of Pompey, at Mylae and Naulochus in 36, and 
2 CONC Mark Antony at Actium in 31. He also did good service in Gaul, Spain, Syria and Pannonia. (Larousse Biographical Dictionary, p 17)
