1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Appius Claudius Pulcher (c. 139 BC – 76 BC) was a Roman politician of the 1st century BC. There is uncertainty about who is father was. It was most probably the Appius Claudius Pulcher who was consul in 143 BC.[1] 
2 CONC He was a supporter of Lucius Cornelius Sulla and served as praetor in 88 BC. He was exiled in that year by Gaius Marius while Sulla was away in the east. He returned to Rome after Lucius Cornelius Cinna died in 84 BC, and served a
2 CONC s consul in 79 BC and as governor of Roman Macedonia from 78 BC to 76 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT This Appius Claudius Pulcher was married to Caecilia Metella Balearica (b. c. 125 BC) and was the father of:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Appius Claudius Pulcher
2 CONT * Gaius Claudius Pulcher
2 CONT * Publius Claudius Pulcher, who changed his name to Publius Clodius
2 CONT * Claudia Tertia, who married Quintus Marcius Rex, referred to as "Clodia Marcii"
2 CONT * Claudia (who changed her name to Clodia), wife of Quintus Caecilius Metellus Celer, therefore referred to as "Clodia Metelli"
2 CONT * Claudia (b. c. 90 BC – aft. 66 BC), first wife of Lucius Licinius Lucullus, whom she divorced in 66 BC; referred to as "Clodia Luculli"
