1 NOTE Caius Octavius IV, Senator-Praetor and Governor of Macedonia, died in 59B.C., belonged to an old and respectable but not distinguished familyfrom Velitrae. He was the son of Caius Octavius III., municipalmagistrate of Velitrae. He
2 CONC  was the son of Caius Octavius II., a militarytribune in Sicily, 226 B.C. His father was Caius Octavius I., son ofEneius Octavius Rufus, the Quaestor, or Chancellor of the Republic,living about 330 B.C., the time of Alexander the 
2 CONC Great, and brother ofEneius Octavius, a Roman Admiral under Scipio Africanus in the SecondPunic War.
2 CONT
