1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Aurelia Cotta (120 BC-54 BC) was the daughter of a Rutilia and the consul of 144, Lucius Aurelius Cotta.  Rutilia is assumed to have been a sister of Publius Rutilius Rufus.  After her husband's death, she married 
2 CONC his brother, Gaius Aurelius Cotta, and as a result, Aurelia had three half-brothers, who later became consuls:  Gaius Aurelius Cotta in 75 BC, Lucius Cotta in 74 BC and Marcus Cotta in 65 BC.  Aurelia married Gaius Julius Caesar (
2 CONC the Elder), and her only son was the famous Gaius Julius Caesar.   She also had two daughters, one of them the grandmother of Augustus.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://romanhistorybooks.typepad.com/roman_history_books_and_m/2006/08/post_1.html
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Her mother Rutilia, was a member of the gens Rutilius cognominated Rufus. They were of consular rank
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aurelia_Cotta
