1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Publius_Claudius_Pulcher_(consul_249_BC)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Publius Claudius Pulcher=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT Publius Claudius Pulcher (d 249 BC/246 BC) (of the Claudii family) was a Roman politician.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Gaius Claudius Centho and brother of the famous politician Appius Claudius Caudex (consul in 264 BC), Publius was the first of the Claudii to be given the cognomen "Pulcher" ("handsome"). He was also the father of Appius Cl
2 CONC audius Pulcher, consul in 212 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Career'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Curule aedile in 253 BC, as consul in 249 he was given command of the Roman fleet during the First Punic War. He lost the Battle of Drepana against the Carthaginians after ignoring a bad omen. According to Valerius Maximus, Sueton
2 CONC ius and Cicero, when the sacred chickens refused to eat, Claudius threw them into the sea, saying "Since they do not wish to eat, let them drink!" (Latin "Bibant, quando esse nollent"). He was recalled to Rome and ordered to appoi
2 CONC nt a dictator; his nomination of his subordinate Marcus Claudius Glicia was overruled. He was tried for incompetence and impiety and was fined, and died soon afterwards, possibly by suicide.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Publius_Claudius_Pulcher_(consul_249_BC)
