1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Tarquinia=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT In Rome's early semi-legendary history, Tarquinia was the daughter of Lucius Tarquinius Priscus, the fifth king of Rome, and brother to Rome's seventh and final king, Lucius Tarquinius Superbus. She was the mother of Lucius Junius
2 CONC  Brutus, who overthrew the monarchy and became one of Rome's first consuls in 509 BC. She had another son, who was put to death by Superbus.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarquinia_(daughter_of_Tarquinius_Priscus)
